A further thought - if you were writing a C program, it might be
simplest to try linking in the canonluj.o file from a jbofihe build
(plus anything else that's needed to get the link to succeed - offhand I
don't know what that would be.)  The 'canonluj' module contains a
function canon_lujvo() that takes a lujvo as input and returns its
constituent gismu/cmavo separated by + signs.  e.g. selkla returns
se+klama.  It's not robust to badly formed lujvo - they are supposed to
be weeded out by the front-end scanning of the input text (i.e. the
algorithm provided stand-alone by vlatai.)

